Experiment-3rd

Aim: To Install Nmap & perform network scans to discover hosts & services using different scan types such as TCP SYN scan & UDP scan.
Tools Required:
• Nmap
• Windows Command Prompt
Theory:
Network Mapper is a network scanning tool used to discover hosts, open ports & services running on a network.
• TCP SYN Scan: It sends SYN packets to determine whether TCP ports are open.
• UDP Scan: It scans UDP ports to identify open or filtered UDP services.
Procedure:
1. Check Nmap Installation
nmap --version
2. Host Discovery
nmap -sn 127.0.0.1
3. TCP SYN Scan
nmap -sS 127.0.0.1
4. UDP Scan
nmap -sU 127.0.0.1

Observations:

• Host Discovery:
The Scan detected the local host & showed that the host is up.
• TCP SYN Scan:
The Scan displayed the TCP ports & their states/services on the local host.
• UDP Scan:
The Scan displayed the UDP ports & their states/services on the local host.

